# FDD 24 review — "24 - Data Collection & Compliance - Request for ID Collection".
# Ingested per abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md.
#
# BOUNDED CONTEXT DETERMINATION: "ID Collection" here means identity/Unique-ID
# matching-and-assignment for a NEW EMPLOYEE being added to a district's Employee
# Roster, via Michigan's Mi-Key master-identity service — NOT a document/credential
# upload feature (that reading was ruled out on the first read of the source). The
# document's own Dependencies section names its actor as "the Staffing Data
# Administrator (Data Collection & Compliance- Staffing Administration 10.0)" and its
# own workflow as "utiliz[ing] the established Employee Roster." Both the staffing and
# iam mied-v3 domain conversions already model this exact flow in detail — staffing
# owns the Staffing-facing UI/API surface (Employee Roster, Add Employee, Person
# Search) and iam owns the Mi-Key matching/Near-Match/Identity-Administrator-worklist
# engine underneath it (staffing-domain.ttl's own words: "Staffing does not call Mi-Key
# directly; IAM owns the matching integration and Identity Administrator worklist
# entirely"). Concretely: staff:Seq_AddNewEmployee and staff:Seq_UpdateEmployeeDemographics
# (staffing-sequences.ttl) are near-verbatim matches for this FDD's own narrative, and
# iam:Seq_BusinessUserRequestNewId / iam:Seq_IdentityAdministratorResolveRequest
# (iam-sequences.ttl) are near-verbatim matches for its Near-Match-resolution Addendum
# stories (24.3.x) and admin-outcome-notification story (24.5.2). Requirements below are
# modeled as cred:-free staff:/iam: satisfiedBy targets accordingly — this FDD is
# confirmatory of an already-well-modeled cross-domain flow, not exploratory (same
# pattern FDD 09's review noted for profpractices). NOTE, correcting a stale comment
# found in staffing-domain.ttl's own header (line ~188, "see iam-sequences.md (not yet
# converted into mied-v3)"): iam-sequences.ttl in fact HAS been converted and contains
# exactly the sequences that comment says are missing — a documentation-staleness finding
# in an existing Phase 1 file, not something this pass corrects there, just flagged here.
#
# Source: "24 - Collection & Compliance - Request for ID.docx" (.md sibling read first).
# Unzipped for word/comments.xml (4 comments total — unusually light; see below),
# word/document.xml (drawing order/captions), word/_rels/document.xml.rels (image
# relationship IDs), word/media (13 images, image1.png-image13.png).
#
# Requirement unit used: the FDD's own "Addendum" section is the only place with real
# story numbering (24.2.1, 24.2.2, 24.3.1-24.3.3, 24.4.1-24.4.2, 24.5.1-24.5.3 — ten
# stories total). The "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS" table (11 rows) is skipped per
# CONVENTIONS.md as a duplicative paraphrase of the same content at coarser grain.
# However — same situation FDD 29's pass already documented for its own "Business
# Specifications" prose — the FDD's PRIMARY functional content (the actual "search for
# existing identity, or create new, submit to Mi-Key, get Match/No-Match/Near-Match,
# proceed to employment reporting" happy path, and the separate "Update Demographics"
# workflow) is described in full, wireframed detail in the un-numbered Business
# Specifications prose section but was NEVER itself promoted into the Addendum's
# numbered scheme (the Addendum jumps straight to edge-case/AC-bearing stories:
# read-only-lock, duplicate check, Near-Match resolution sub-steps, file/API upload
# validation, and alerting — never the base "add employee" or "update demographics"
# stories themselves). Modeled below as two synthetic Requirements
# (staff:Req_24_BizSpec_1, staff:Req_24_BizSpec_2) rather than silently left ungraphed,
# consistent with FDD 29's cred:Req_29_BizSpec_* precedent for the exact same situation.
#
# Comments (4 total, via comments.xml): two are a stale-hyperlink correction (not
# load-bearing, folded into the SourceDocument note only). The other two (IDs 35/36,
# Caswell -> Groom "Confirmed") are substantive and drove the coverage-gap Annotation
# on Feature 24.4 below (bulk-update-of-existing-IDs and direct-district-to-Mi-Key API
# scope are both still explicitly undefined in the FDD's own text, and the reviewer
# comment thread confirms rather than resolves that). No tracked changes found worth
# reconstructing.
#
# Wireframes: 13 images total. The 5 individually captioned ones (image1.png-image5.png,
# confirmed in document order immediately following their own drawing anchor, then
# followed by the caption paragraph — verified by viewing all 5, not assumed) are
# extracted as wireframes/wireframe-01 through -05. The remaining 8 (image6.png-image13.png,
# embedded directly in the Addendum's acceptance-criteria bullets with no caption text at
# all) were ALL individually viewed given the small total count (13, well under FDD
# 11/16 or 29's image volumes) — extracted as wireframes/wireframe-06 through -13.
#
# NOTABLE CROSS-CHECK FINDING: wireframe-06 ("ID Management Requests" list) and
# wireframe-08/09/10 (the three Near-Match resolution action variants: Create New ID,
# Match & Link IDs, Deny Request) all carry a "< Back to Rapbacks" breadcrumb and the
# screen title "ID Collection Request #122456" — i.e. the actual product UI files this
# FDD's own Identity-Administrator worklist screens under a "Rapbacks" navigation
# section. Neither this FDD's own text nor iam-domain.ttl/iam-sequences.ttl ever uses
# the word "Rapback" anywhere — FDD 30 (Rapbacks) is itself still unreviewed (per
# fdd-review/STATUS.md's "not yet done" list). This is left as an open discrepancy
# Annotation rather than assumed to mean anything definite about FDD 30's scope, since
# FDD 30 hasn't been reviewed to confirm or deny the connection.
#
# Verification-in-passing: wireframe-11/12 (Upload Employee Roster modal + its "Line 12
# - No UID / Line 23 - No UID / Line 137 - Duplicate UID" error result) are a striking,
# independent visual confirmation of staffing-permissions.ttl's own already-documented
# staff:Perm_EmployeeRosterBulkUpload gap (a Permission that exists with NO backing
# sd:ApiOperation anywhere in staffing-api.ttl) — this FDD's own 24.4.1 describes
# exactly the validation behavior the wireframe shows, reinforcing rather than
# resolving that pre-existing, real coverage gap. See Req_24_4_1 below.
#
# CONFIRMED CROSS-FDD OVERLAP WITH FDD 15.2 (per the concurrently-completed FDD 15
# review's own flag): FDD 24's own Business Specifications prose literally cites "15.2 -
# Business User Request for ID Requirements.docx" as the workflow spec it follows ("The
# system will follow the workflow requirements between MiEdWorkforce and Mi-Key as
# defined: 15.2..."), and fdd-review/15-identity-management-integration.ttl's own
# iam:Req_15_2_1 note independently flags a source-document reviewer comment
# cross-referencing "24.2.1" (this FDD) as a live duplicate-effort risk. Having now
# reviewed both: the overlap is REAL and BY DESIGN, not an error — FDD 15.2 is IAM's own
# detailed inbound spec for the identical "search-or-create, submit to Mi-Key, Match/
# No-Match/Near-Match" mechanics that FDD 24 re-describes from the Staffing-side UI/
# business-process perspective. Concretely, staff:Req_24_BizSpec_1 (this file) and
# iam:Req_15_2_1/15_2_2/15_2_3 (the FDD 15 file) are near-verbatim restatements of the
# same underlying capability, and both independently resolve to the SAME satisfiedBy
# targets (iam:Seq_BusinessUserRequestNewId, iam:Op_SubmitBusinessUserIdentityRequest,
# iam:IdentityResolutionCompletedEvent) — genuine convergent confirmation from two
# separately-authored source FDDs, not duplicated graph nodes (each keeps its own FDD's
# own requirementId per CONVENTIONS.md; no attempt is made here to merge or supersede
# either file). One difference worth flagging for whoever next touches FDD 15's own
# Person-Search gap (iam:Question_PersonSearchNotModeled, per that file's own Req_15_2_1
# note): FDD 24's wireframe 1 (this file) shows a real, wireframed Person Search screen
# with a broader field set (Unique ID/First/Last/Email/Credential number/Application
# number/DOB/SSN) than FDD 15.2's own AC text describes (Unique ID exact-match or Name/
# SSN/CLN) — additional wireframe-only evidence for that same still-open gap, not itself
# closing it.

